### Summary

I found one fix-level bug and two lower-severity items in the cached-first default-branch resolution and the manager's background fetch. The main bug: for a repo whose remote has just received its first push, the first start can be seeded from the local initial commit. Reading the code, the fetch skip and background-fetch logic otherwise holds up, and the new tests match what the code does.

